updater: prereleases from a URL feed (beta directory)

Patch 0003 gave apps a beta channel on GitHub: SetPrereleases(true) finds
the newest prerelease or release through the GitHub API. Updates from a
`url` (with or without `updates.s3`) still had a single manifest, so an
app moving its updates from GitHub to its own site lost its beta channel.
A feed served from a URL now has a beta directory beside it, by
convention, with no new setting:

  https://dl.example.com/app/update-darwin-arm64.json       releases
  https://dl.example.com/app/beta/update-darwin-arm64.json  prereleases

- internal/update: PrereleaseFeed(feed) names the beta manifest of a URL
  feed (false for GitHub feeds, whose prereleases ResolvePrereleaseFeed
  finds); PrereleaseDir = "beta".
- Check with SetPrereleases(true) reads both manifests and offers the
  newer version; a missing beta manifest (404) falls back to the
  releases' one silently, another failure with a log line; a 404 is told
  apart by a statusError (same message as before). Without prereleases
  the beta manifest is never asked for.
- `mygo build`: the archive and delta URLs of a prerelease version point
  into beta/ (the feed linked into the app stays the releases'); deltas
  are made from both manifests, as on GitHub.
- `mygo build -upload` to S3: a prerelease goes under <prefix>/beta/,
  manifests last; a release also writes its manifests to beta/, last,
  unless a newer prerelease is published there (or it cannot be read:
  then it warns), so the beta manifest names the newest of either kind.

Tests: TestPrereleaseFeed, TestUpdaterURLPrereleases (newer of the two,
404 and 503 fallbacks, only prereleases, beta never read when off,
install), TestWriteDeltasURLPrereleases (URLs in beta/, deltas from both),
TestPublishS3 (release writes beta/ unless newer or unreadable; a
prerelease goes in beta/).
